.TH ADI2-CONTROL 1 "November 2026" "rme-adi2-control 1.1.0" "User Commands"
.SH NAME
adi2-control \- remote control and EQ builder for RME ADI-2 DACs
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B adi2-control
.SH DESCRIPTION
.B adi2-control
opens a GTK4 window that reads and writes the settings of an RME ADI-2 DAC,
ADI-2 Pro or ADI-2/4 Pro over USB MIDI SysEx, including a graphical
5-band parametric EQ for each output. Without a connected unit it works as an
offline EQ profile builder.
.PP
Turn on MIDI Control in the unit's setup menu and connect it by USB. The app
finds the ALSA raw MIDI port with
.BR amidi (1)
and reconnects when the unit is switched on.
.SH FILES
.TP
.I ~/.config/rme-adi2/profiles/
Local EQ profiles, as JSON.
.TP
.I /usr/share/rme-adi2-control/profiles/
Bundled EQ profiles.
.TP
.I /usr/share/doc/rme-adi2-control/examples/pipewire/
Optional PipeWire and WirePlumber drop-ins for bit-perfect playback.
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR adi2-eq (1),
.BR amidi (1)
